The Master of Ceremonies is a tall, slender elf in an elaborate high-collared coat adorned with a striking blue-and-gold diamond harlequin pattern, his face concealed behind a pale, unblinking mask with small elegant horns. The mask has slits for the eyes and mouth, and he wears large red gems full of magic and a metal bracer on his left arm with a firearm set into it, set so that it can be seen.

He leads [[Org/The Harlequins/index|The Harlequins]], the builders of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] and the organizers of the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]], and he hears the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] himself. When he lifts the mask, his face is scar tissue with no feature left, as if he had burned to death and been healed only partway, and he carries the copper and sulfur smell of a fiend; the reading of him places him with the devil called [[Divinity/Fiends/The Harlequin|the Harlequin]].

He receives guests aboard the strider one at a time and tells them little. He says [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari Vaino]] is still alive and that what has become of Illmari is not his story to tell. He wants to know what waits at the end of the journey, and expects the nineteen organizations aboard to come to blows along the way, which he says he will encourage because he would be bored otherwise. He has favorites, and says no one wants to be one of them.

At the banquet the evening the Providence left Ragged Roost he asked the guests for a weekly tithe of energy to drive the pilgrimage, warning that a guest who could not pay it would suffer.
